<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<style>
  * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  body {
    font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
    background: #0f1117;
    color: #e2e4e9;
    padding: 28px 32px;
    min-height: 100vh;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #ffffff;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
    letter-spacing: -0.3px;
  }
  .subtitle {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #8b8f9a;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .bullets {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
  }
  .bullet {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 12px;
    background: #181a22;
    border: 1px solid #252833;
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 14px 16px;
  }
  .bullet-icon {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .icon-blue  { background: #1e3a5f; color: #5b9bf5; }
  .icon-green { background: #1a3d2e; color: #4ade80; }
  .icon-amber { background: #3d2e1a; color: #f59e0b; }
  .bullet-text h3 {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #f0f1f4;
    margin-bottom: 3px;
  }
  .bullet-text p {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: #9ca0ab;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  .scorecard {
    background: #181a22;
    border: 1px solid #252833;
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 18px 20px;
  }
  .scorecard h2 {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #8b8f9a;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.6px;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .score-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    padding: 8px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #1e2029;
  }
  .score-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .score-label {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #c4c7cf;
    min-width: 140px;
  }
  .score-bar-wrap {
    flex: 1;
    margin: 0 14px;
    height: 8px;
    background: #252833;
    border-radius: 4px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .score-bar {
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: 4px;
    transition: width 0.6s ease;
  }
  .bar-blue   { background: #5b9bf5; }
  .bar-green  { background: #4ade80; }
  .bar-amber  { background: #f59e0b; }
  .bar-purple { background: #a78bfa; }
  .bar-rose   { background: #fb7185; }
  .score-val {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #e2e4e9;
    min-width: 36px;
    text-align: right;
  }
  .footer {
    margin-top: 20px;
    font-size: 11.5px;
    color: #555a66;
    text-align: center;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<h1>OpenCloset Eval Harness</h1>
<p class="subtitle">Why a structured evaluation layer matters for the workspace</p>

<div class="bullets">
  <div class="bullet">
    <div class="bullet-icon icon-blue">1</div>
    <div class="bullet-text">
      <h3>Ground-truth regression guard</h3>
      <p>Catches silent quality drift before it ships â every prompt variant, every agent turn, measured against known expectations.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="bullet">
    <div class="bullet-icon icon-green">2</div>
    <div class="bullet-text">
      <h3>Comparative model scoring</h3>
      <p>Side-by-side evals across providers and versions so you pick the right model for the task, not just the cheapest.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="bullet">
    <div class="bullet-icon icon-amber">3</div>
    <div class="bullet-text">
      <h3>Reproducible benchmarking</h3>
      <p>Snapshot datasets, deterministic scoring, and versioned results â the harness is the single source of truth for quality claims.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="scorecard">
  <h2>Scorecard</h2>
  <div class="score-row">
    <span class="score-label">Prompt Faithfulness</span>
    <div class="score-bar-wrap"><div class="score-bar bar-blue" style="width:87%"></div></div>
    <span class="score-val">87</span>
  </div>
  <div class="score-row">
    <span class="score-label">Tool Use Accuracy</span>
    <div class="score-bar-wrap"><div class="score-bar bar-green" style="width:92%"></div></div>
    <span class="score-val">92</span>
  </div>
  <div class="score-row">
    <span class="score-label">Context Window Handling</span>
    <div class="score-bar-wrap"><div class="score-bar bar-amber" style="width:74%"></div></div>
    <span class="score-val">74</span>
  </div>
  <div class="score-row">
    <span class="score-label">Multi-turn Consistency</span>
    <div class="score-bar-wrap"><div class="score-bar bar-purple" style="width:81%"></div></div>
    <span class="score-val">81</span>
  </div>
  <div class="score-row">
    <span class="score-label">Error Recovery</span>
    <div class="score-bar-wrap"><div class="score-bar bar-rose" style="width:68%"></div></div>
    <span class="score-val">68</span>
  </div>
</div>

<p class="footer">Scores are illustrative placeholders â real values come from the harness run.</p>

</body>
</html>
</transient-window>

